<title>CHINA: African Development Bank launches 30 bln yen bond.</title>
<headline>African Development Bank launches 30 bln yen bond.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The African Development Bank has launched a 30 billion yen subordinated Eurobond to be priced later on Wednesday in London, lead manager Goldman Sachs said.</p>
<p>The bond matures in August 2002 and will be priced to yield 22 basis points over the Japanese Government Bond 148.</p>
<p>Fees are 25 basis points.</p>
<p>The issue is rated Aa1 by Moody's Investors Service and AA-minus by Standard and Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
